# .gitleaksignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Baseline of known-safe findings, keyed by Gitleaks fingerprint
# (commit:file:rule:line). Read automatically by gitleaks/gitleaks-action and
# by the bare `gitleaks` CLI -- no extra flag needed.
#
# Why this file exists: `.gitleaks.toml`'s path-based allowlist covers
# `infra-vm/terraform.tfvars.example` as it exists in the *current* tree, but
# `fetch-depth: 0` in ci.yml makes Gitleaks walk the *entire* commit history
# (see ci.yml's "Gitleaks secret scan" job). Commit d2d18d4 predates that
# allowlist / the file's current name-or-shape, so the path regex doesn't
# retroactively match it there, and the placeholder `cloudflare_origin_cert_key`
# PEM block (never a real key -- see .gitleaks.toml's own header comment for
# the full story) keeps tripping the generic "private-key" rule on every scan.
# Ignoring the exact historical fingerprint below is the standard way to
# permanently clear a confirmed-safe historical finding without rewriting
# repo history (which would break every existing clone/fork).
#
# If Gitleaks ever reports a *different* fingerprint for this same file/line
# (e.g. because the commit hash changes after a history rewrite), add the new
# fingerprint here rather than editing the old line.
d2d18d45633883499bb5c825e6b8766d1f6e528b:infra-vm/terraform.tfvars.example:private-key:44
